   "function": "Programmable Unijunction Transistor — the IN CAL latch. Anode fed from the Q5 (+BRIDGE) node through R15 (51 kΩ) and then R14 (150 kΩ); gate tied to the R15/R14 junction (the latch node) through R16 (1 MΩ) with C6 across it, and to RESET (P2-19) through R23 (270 kΩ); cathode drives the Q6 base, bypassed to P2-20 by C7. Touching RESET to COMMON pulls the gate below the anode and fires it; it then conducts as long as Q5 supplies the node. When the supply fails it turns off and, when power is restored, remains latched off until its gate is pulled down again via RESET (§3-16: 'until its emitter is connected momentarily to the COMMON output terminal via the RESET connection'; §2-26; Procedure A step 19, §4-37, PDF p34).",
